.TH KERYKEION 1 "" "kerykeion-cli 6.0.0rc1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kerykeion \- astrology from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kerykeion
.RI [ global\-flags ]
.I command
.RI [ command\-flags ]
.PP
.B python \-m kerykeion_cli
.I [the same arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Astrology from the terminal. Save a subject once (kerykeion subject save
ada \-\-date 1990\-07\-15 \-\-time 10:30 \-\-lat 41.9 \-\-lng 12.5
\-\-tz Europe/Rome), then pass \-s ada to any command. A terminal gets a
text report, a pipe gets JSON; \-f text|json|xml|svg and \-o FILE choose
explicitly.
.PP
The payload always goes to stdout and warnings always to stderr, in
every format, so a piped payload stays clean.
.PP
The engine is the library itself, in\-process and offline: no key, no
server. Save a subject once (kerykeion subject save NAME ...) and pass
\-s NAME to any command that needs one.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
These go before the command. A bare \fBkerykeion\fR prints help and exits 0.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the kerykeion\-cli version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-traceback
Show a full traceback on error (default: a one\-line message).
.TP
.B \-\-warnings\-as\-errors
Exit 9 when any ephemeris warning or house fallback occurs.
.SH COMMANDS
The tree below is generated from the same parser behind \-\-help, so it
