kerykeion <command> \-\-help, and kerykeion info lists every value the
value\-taking flags accept.
.TP
.B kerykeion natal [flags]
Natal chart: text report, JSON, XML or SVG.
.TP
.B kerykeion now [flags]
Chart of the current moment at a place.
.TP
.B kerykeion synastry [flags]
Synastry of two stored subjects (dual wheel).
.TP
.B kerykeion transit [flags]
Natal chart against a transit moment (dual wheel).  The moment defaults
to now at the natal birthplace (offline). Pass \-\-lat/\-\-lng/\-\-tz
for a relocated transit, or \-\-city to geocode; pass \-\-to\-date and
\-\-to\-time together for a specific moment.
.TP
.B kerykeion composite [flags]
Midpoint composite of two stored subjects.
.TP
.B kerykeion return [flags]
Solar or lunar return for a year (dual wheel).  Cast for the natal
birthplace by default (offline). Relocate with \-\-lat/\-\-lng/\-\-tz or
with \-\-city \-\-nation (geocoded), never both.
.TP
.B kerykeion progression [flags]
Secondary progression to a target year (dual wheel).
.TP
.B kerykeion aspects [flags]
Aspects within a chart, or between two (\-S).  Declination aspects take
a single \-\-orb and have no per\-aspect table or axis rule, so
\-\-aspects and \-\-axis\-orb\-limit are rejected there.
.TP
.B kerykeion dominants [flags]
Dominant signs, elements, qualities and planets.
