.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.TP
.B text
the ASCII report (the default on a terminal)
.TP
.B json
the Pydantic model_dump_json() payload (the default in a pipe)
.TP
.B xml
the to_context() document, the compact LLM\-oriented serialisation
.TP
.B svg
an SVG chart wheel (chart commands)
.PP
Resolution order: \-f, then the suffix of \-o, then
$KERYKEION_CLI_FORMAT, then the terminal\-or\-pipe default. \-\-envelope
wraps a JSON payload with the version, backend and warnings for a
consumer that only captures stdout.
.SH SUBJECT PROFILES
A profile is a small JSON recipe (written 0600, in a 0700 directory:
birth data is personal) under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kerykeion/subjects/.
subject save writes one; subject list, subject show, subject path and
subject verify inspect it; \-s <name> (and \-S for a second subject)
reuses it everywhere. A profile is a recipe, never a cached chart: every
read rebuilds the subject, so it cannot go stale across versions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KERYKEION_CLI_FORMAT
the default output format when \-f and \-o are absent (text, json, xml
or svg).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
root of the profile store; defaults to ~/.config when unset.
.PP
The ephemeris backend is configured through the environment too;
KERYKEION_BACKEND, KERYKEION_LEB_MODE, KERYKEION_EPHE_PATH,
LIBEPHEMERIS_MODE, LIBEPHEMERIS_DATA_DIR, LIBEPHEMERIS_LEB,
LIBEPHEMERIS_PRECISION select and shape it, and kerykeion status reports
which values are in effect.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kerykeion/subjects/*.json
the stored subject profiles.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes are the contract: branch on the code, never on the message
text.
.TP
.B 0
OK: success.
.TP
.B 1
UNEXPECTED: a bug; rerun with \-\-traceback to see it.
.TP
.B 2
usage: the argument parser rejected the command line.
.TP
.B 4
INVALID_INPUT: a flag or value is wrong; the message names it.
.TP
.B 5
KERYKEION_ERROR: the library refused the request.
.TP
.B 6
EPHEMERIS: outside ephemeris coverage, or the data files are unusable.
.TP
.B 7
NETWORK: GeoNames unreachable.
.TP
.B 8
SAMPLING_LIMIT: the series exceeds the sampling ceiling; nothing was
computed.
.TP
.B 9
WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS: warnings were made fatal by
\-\-warnings\-as\-errors.
.TP
.B 130
INTERRUPTED: Ctrl\-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Save a subject once, then reuse it everywhere with \-s
.RS 4
.nf
kerykeion subject save ada \-\-name "Ada Lovelace" \-\-date 1900\-12\-10 \-\-time 18:00 \(rs
    \-\-lat 51.5074 \-\-lng \-0.1278 \-\-tz Europe/London \-\-offline
kerykeion natal \-s ada
.fi
.RE
.PP
A terminal gets the text report, a pipe gets JSON \- no extra flag
.RS 4
.nf
kerykeion natal \-s ada | jq \-r .sun.sign
.fi
.RE
.PP
An SVG wheel, themed, written to a file
.RS 4
.nf
kerykeion natal \-s ada \-f svg \-o ada.svg \-\-theme dark
.fi
.RE
.PP
A year of transits, as events
.RS 4
.nf
kerykeion transits \-s ada \-\-from 2026\-01\-01 \-\-to 2026\-12\-31 \-\-events
.fi
.RE
.PP
Ask the CLI what a flag accepts, read from the library at runtime
.RS 4
.nf
kerykeion info literals SiderealMode
.fi
.RE
.PP
Judge the install (exit 6 when it is genuinely broken)
.RS 4
.nf
kerykeion status \-\-check
.fi
.RE
